# The live blog, oldest first.
#
# A line here is an articles/<slug> directory in this repository, and it is also
# the URL: rakuensoftware.com/blog/<slug>. Adding a line and merging it to main
# is what publishing is. The site polls this branch and ships the change within
# a few minutes; nothing else has to be deployed.
#
# This list used to live in the site repository, so publishing meant a commit
# here and a second commit there. It moved on 2026-08-20 to put the decision
# next to the article it is about.
#
# Before that it was not a list at all, but a test: an article was published if
# its markdown carried frontmatter. Every article here carries frontmatter,
# including the ready-but-unpublished ones and the drafts whose own provenance
# maps say their figures do not reproduce, so on 2026-08-12 a deploy put eleven
# of them on the live site at once. The rule was silent about it: the build
# succeeded, the count went up, and nothing named what was new.
#
# A file property cannot carry that decision, because the property is a side
# effect of how articles are written and the decision belongs to a person.
# Writing the line is the decision. Everything absent is held on purpose.
#
# Removing a line retires a live URL, which the site refuses to do unless its
# build is run with ALLOW_UNPUBLISH=1. Renaming one changes a live URL and
# breaks every inbound link to it. The slug is the directory name, not the
# article's `slug:` frontmatter field.

